# The Bratislava new-build market is growing in supply and in sales, prices are standing still

The last two months on the Bratislava new-build market brought stronger demand, price stagnation and an increase in the number of flats for sale. Sales rose from {qSalesThen} to {qSalesNow} flats against the previous period. The price level was unchanged and moved by {qPanelM2ChangePctEn}% on a comparable sample of projects. The supply of flats for sale rose to {qSupply}.

As of {asOfEn} the supply on the new-build market consisted, according to Residata's analysts, of {qSupply} flats across {qProjects} projects. Against the position {qPanelDays} days earlier, supply rose by {qPanelSupplyChange} flats or {qPanelSupplyChangePctEn}%, the comparison being computed on the sample of {qPanelProjects} projects we track at both dates.

The average price of these flats on offer reached {qMeanM2} €/m² incl. VAT, which on the comparable sample of projects is a change of only {qPanelM2ChangePctEn}%. It can be said that new-build prices are currently moving at a pace close to zero, and that differences in the average price are caused by the composition of supply rather than by movements in price lists. Over the last two months {qNewUnits} flats were added to the offer at an average price of {qNewMeanM2} €/m² incl. VAT, that is below the market level, which slightly lowers the average price.

The average absolute price of flats on offer stood at {qMeanPrice} € incl. VAT, while their average floor area reached {qMeanAreaEn} m².

